Jeremy Matthew Toeman <Shaggy+@CMU.EDU> writes:
>What are the easiest ways to identify the following:
>1] Rings

Wear them, or drop them down a sink.

>2] Wands

Zap them, or engrave with them.

>3] Potions

Drink them. Or dip a unicorn horn in them.

>4] Scrolls

Read them.

>How can you tell if food is tainted?

If your pet won't eat it; if it's been more than a few turns since you killed
it.

>How many entrances to the Mines are there?

One.

>What should you not eat (like humans and pets), and why not?

Generally, you shouldn't eat your own race or a pet because your god'll
get mad at you; there's several things that are poisonous, but if you have
resist poison you'll be fine. Tainted food will kill you quick, so you'll
have to #pray...

>What is the point of carrying gems?

Ups your score; you can throw them at unicorns; portable wealth (they're
much lighter than gold).

>How do you get Dragon Scale armor?

You need to either find it or find some dragon scales.

>What creatures should you not kill (like guards), and why not?

Peaceful creatures. Because your god'll get mad at you.

>How can you tell if your god is pissed at you?

By sacrificing at an altar (and watching the signs); by praying (but if he
is pissed, this is dangerous).

